@baseUrl = http://localhost:8082
@csrfToken = paste-token-from-csrf-response

### Run this GET first, copy its token into @csrfToken above, then send the POST requests one by one. IntelliJ keeps the session cookie in its HTTP Client cookie jar.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/csrf

### Register a demo user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "email": "csrf.demo@example.com",
  "password": "ChangeMe123!"
}

### Log in as the demo user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

{
  "email": "csrf.demo@example.com",
  "password": "ChangeMe123!"
}

### Check which user is authenticated in this session
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### Log out and invalidate the session
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
X-CSRF-TOKEN: {{csrfToken}}

### After logout, this should return 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me